PROBE (a), REGRESSED real 4 -> 15, insns T50/O51, --ops `target-only: +2 blt / ours-only: -2 bge -1 li`, reverted. Helper with TWO early exits:

static inline u8* sSoundDataEntry(int idx) {
    u8* e;
    if (idx < 0) { return 0; }
    e = *(u8**)(gWorldData + 44) + idx * 24;
    if (*(s32*)(e + offsetof(struct sound_data, idx)) < 0) { return 0; }
    return e;
}

MWCC did NOT tail-merge the two `return 0;` sites: the first materialised its own `li r3,0` plus a branch at +0x1c (--ops `O[7:10]@1c-28=['bge','li','b']` against `T[7:8]@1c-20=['blt']`), so ours gained an instruction and lost count parity.

PROBE (b), KEPT, byte-exact. Same helper with a SINGLE trailing zero exit -- the failure paths fall out of the guarded block instead of each returning:

static inline u8* sSoundDataEntry(int idx) {
    if (idx >= 0) {
        u8* e = *(u8**)(gWorldData + 44) + idx * 24;
        if (*(s32*)(e + offsetof(struct sound_data, idx)) >= 0) {
            return e;
        }
    }
    return 0;
}

Call site: `u8* entry = sSoundDataEntry(level->entersnd);` replacing the `switch (entry_id) { case 0: goto valid_entry; default: ... }` carrier a prior probe had left in the tree.
